Data Lake - Evotion because of the Big Data 
		  - Unstructured / Semi structure / Strucutered 
Data Warehouse  - Structured data (99%) / Properly aligned data  for the reporting and the analysis 
Data Mart - This is the conformed structure of the the data which get utilized by the downstream aPPLICATION 


------------------------

OLTP - complex stystem , OL transactional processing , recent data  , R/W operations, Responses in the milliseconds, less maintainence, more 	normalized (upto 3NF), No SQLDb (Dynamo DB, Cosmos Db, Mongo DB)

OLAP - OL analytical processing,Contains all hiostorical data , more denormalized, data is mostly red (Update frequency is very less), filtereed and cleaned, Analytical reporting, complex queries, do not keep raw data, and only strucutred data, uses columner db / systems for the  data storage,
ETL,  Not a live data. 

---------------------------------

Data Load strategies : -  

1 : Full/ Truncate Load -  Load the whole data from OLTP --> OLAP systems (trucate the target table and load the entire source to target)
2 : Incremental/ Delta Load - Load the changed data from OLTP --> OLAP systems (Load only the changed or new record to the target system)

----------------------------------

Measures - Quantitative property of  the DW , can be calculated, logical meaning for the aggregations
	Types of measure : 
		1. Additive : Summed / aggregated across all the dimensions 
		2. Semi-additive : Agrregated across the some of the dimensions
		3. Non-additive : Can not be agregated across any dimensions 
	Measures goes into the fact table 99% 
	Every number is not the measure like "room_number"
Attributes - Helps defining measures, "total sales (measures) per month(attribute)"
	Grain : To design data warehouse we need to define the grain
		  : Level of the measurement like per day, per month, total sales per store #Grain atomicity 
		  : Calculated from low level grain((per day) to the high level gain (per month) 
	KPI : Key perfomance indicator, main  reason to design the DW 
		: Requirements compes from the KPI
		: Measurable value for the company performance
	Attributes goes into the dimensions table 
	
---------------------------------------

Fact and dimensions 

Dimensions : 
	1. Conformed dimensions: It is the dimensions shared across the multiple fact tables and hold the same meaning across all. 
				: Can be determined using bus metrics
	2. Junk Dimensions : It is the single dimension table that holds the low cardinality flags, indicator, codes , boolean columns 
						 that are related  to the fact table row but do not belogs to any other existing dimensions. 
					   : Instead of storing the 8 separate flag columns directely on the fact table, combine them into the junk dimension table 
						 with a single surrogate key and store only that one integewr key on the fact table
	3. Role Playing Dmensions : A single physical dimension table that is referenced mul;tiple times by the same fact table, with each 
								referenced representing the different meaning. 
							  : e.g : A date dimension referenced three times in the sales fact table - like (order_date , ship_date, delivery_date)
	4. Degenerated Dimensions : A dimension attribute that is stores directly on the fact table because it has no corresponding dimension table and 
								it does not make sense to create the dimension table for that dimension attributes.
	5. Slowly Changing Dimensions :  
		1.SCD Type 1 : Upsert and Incremental Updates
					 : Only Current Change No History 
					 : Overwrite
		2.SCD Type 2 : Incremental Loads ,
					 : Maintain all the history using introduced column (flag, starty date and end date) 
		3.SCD Type 3 : Least used 
					 : Holds the current and the last change 
					 
					 
-------------------------------

Surrogate Key : Artifical key, doesnt exists, does not hold any business value 
Natural Key   : Unique , Holds business value, existed in the real world

####
How surrogate key are loaded in the DW 
In actual scenario mostly dimensions are loaded before facts.

------------------------------------
Fact table fundamental :
	:it is central table in the star schema records the measures in t it. 
	:Every row represent the one instace of the declared grain - one event, one period , one pipeline stage. 
	:Fact table has threee typesof the column : FK, measure columns, degenerated dimensions columns 
Types : : : 

1. Transactional Fact Table :  One row per event at a point in time 
2. Periodic snapshot Table : One row per entity per period 
3. Accumulating snapshot table : One row per entity lifecycle instaces 
4. Factless fact table : Froregin key only, no numeric measures 
		1.Event Factless Fact Table : Recording Occurence  - Records that an even t happened to the specific entity at a specific time.
									: The event itself is the business fact , there is no quantity or the amount to be measure
		2.Coverage Factless Fact Table : Defining Eligibility - Records what COULD Happen - not what DID Happen 
									   : It enables "What should have happened but didn't?"
